# The clockwise square: mirror of square.tour (same 600 mm sides, four
# legs straight through) with every turn NEGATIVE omega.
#
# Why it exists: the rotation calibration carries SEPARATE gains for
# positive and negative turns (rotation_gain_pos / rotation_gain_neg), so
# a CCW-only square can never see a per-direction asymmetry. Run both
# squares; compare their closures.
#
# CW mirror: occupies 0..+600 in x and 0..-600 in y from its start, so
# stage at (-300, +300) facing East to sit centred. Sizing, pivot speed
# and the removal of the ported mid-leg STOPs / SET block: see
# square.tour (2026-09-06).

MARK leg1
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=-180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg2
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=-180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg3
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=-180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg4
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=-180 angle=90 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.5
